  message: "BRANCH WORK 2026-10-04 (not integrated, no status change): branch jgstern-agent/fix/napaf, worktree ~/hg_wt/napaf, commit 09f38364f8. Full report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/napaf.md.\nFix: the receiverless branch of ruby.py's call arm now ends in make_unresolved_edge(\"ruby\", ...) -> ruby:external:0-0:<name>:unresolved (python's INV-foluz residual / WI-fahod shape, no call_construct) when local symbols and the resolver miss. No local-binding refusal is needed: a receiverless tree-sitter `call` has args, parens or a block, and in ruby that is a send to self even with a same-named local (x = 1; x(2) is NoMethodError). super(...) is excluded by node type.\nTests: test_ruby_receiverless_unresolved.py, 3 red before / 6 green after; board smart-test (296 affected files): 9759 passed, 0 failed, 2 xfailed, ruby.py 100% coverage, mypy ratchet clean.\nCorpus A/B by call site (survey, frozen copies, own XDG, code-under-test printed per arm): postal +2,330, chatwoot +6,442, mastodon +20,520 sites, all ruby:external; 0 removed, 0 other changes; 55-69% in spec/ (RSpec DSL). 0 io tags in either arm (ruby ships no catalogue). Compact-view node selection shifts slightly via centrality (postal 64k 7/12 swapped, mastodon 64k 15/15); not judged.\nWI-javaf hazard: in ruby the short-name reach of `external` to a function-kind Kernel row is the WANTED outcome (Kernel is ambient); a shadowing project method resolves first. Both pinned via classify_call with a Kernel.system overlay row.\nResidual silent shapes (bare identifier calls, untyped variable receiver, AMB-METHOD, super, recursion) filed as WI-misir-runir-danil-sugad-vovan-kotid-nipav-rabim."  # 8514
